  "answer": "### Short Answer\nThe estate tax rate under the Tax Reform for Acceleration and Inclusion (TRAIN) law is a flat rate of 6% on the value of the estate exceeding Five Million Pesos (₱5,000,000).\n\n### Interpretation\nSection 84 of the NIRC specifies that the estate tax is imposed on the net estate of a decedent, which is the gross estate less allowable deductions. The flat rate of 6% applies only to the portion of the estate that exceeds the threshold of ₱5,000,000.\n\n### Practical Meaning\nIn practical terms, if a decedent's estate is valued at ₱10,000,000, the taxable estate would be ₱5,000,000 (₱10,000,000 - ₱5,000,000), resulting in an estate tax liability of ₱300,000 (6% of ₱5,000,000). This simplified tax structure aims to streamline estate tax compliance and reduce the burden on estates below the threshold.",
